Item 5.03 Amendments to Articles of Incorporation or Bylaws; Change in Fiscal Year

On November 18, 2026, the Board of Directors (the “Board”) of Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. (the “Company”) approved amendments to the Company’s amended and restated bylaws (as amended and restated, the “Bylaws”), effective immediately. Among other things, the amendments to the Bylaws:

•allow the Company to disregard votes for any nominee submitted by a stockholder that did not comply with the universal proxy rules adopted by the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, including the requirement for stockholder proponents to solicit holders of at least 67% of the voting power;

•clarify and enhance procedural mechanics and disclosure requirements in connection with stockholder director nominations and business proposals at stockholder meetings, including, without limitation, to:

◦update the required background information and disclosures regarding proposing and nominating stockholders, proposed nominees and business, and certain persons related to a stockholder’s solicitation of proxies;

◦permit the Board to reasonably request additional information from proposing and nominating stockholders; and

◦clarify the obligation of proposing and nominating stockholders and proposed nominees to update and supplement notices;

•provide that any stockholder soliciting proxies from other stockholders must use a proxy card color other than white;

•clarify the authority of the chair of a stockholder meeting and the inspectors of election;

•provide that the number of directors is fixed solely by Board resolution and that vacancies and newly created directorships may be filled only by the directors, unless otherwise provided in the Company’s Certificate of Incorporation;

•update the exclusive forum provision to add other Delaware state courts and the U.S. District Court for the District of Delaware as fallback forums if the Court of Chancery lacks jurisdiction and add enforcement procedures…
